# Exemptions from the shared instance-data gate. Format: "<scan label>: <ERE>".
# Each applies to the named scan only. Add a reason; an exemption without one is
# indistinguishable from a mistake six months later.
#
# This file is tracked and therefore scanned like any other. Keep the reasons free
# of forms the scans catch — spelling one out here would need an exemption of its own.
#
# Patterns are tested against git grep output, so they see "path:line:content".
# Anchoring with ^ matches the path, not the text — write the pattern unanchored.

# Design notes and plans carry their date in the filename, and the index links them by
# that name. A metadata field records when a document was written. The heuristic reads
# a research word next to a date as a narrated session; in both of these it is a title
# and a field, and the prose beside them is already free of local paths.
dated observation: docs/[a-z0-9-]+-[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}\.md|audited_at:

# The SSRF regression tests must name addresses from the ranges the guard refuses; they are
# documentation-style stand-ins for reserved ranges, not addresses of any real host.
private address: tests/test_ssrf\.py:
